00:35:35.570 --> 00:35:37.810
whereas through the camp cultural club,

00:35:37.810 --> 00:35:40.580
we have women and men working together

00:35:40.580 --> 00:35:42.150
from different generations

00:35:42.150 --> 00:35:44.500
to identify what some
of these gaps would be,

00:35:44.500 --> 00:35:47.900
whether it's information,
food, financial resources,

00:35:47.900 --> 00:35:52.900
sanitation products or stepping
in to provide those medical,

00:35:54.740 --> 00:35:58.420
medical resources or access
to those medical resources.

00:35:58.420 --> 00:36:02.230
I'm looking forward to delving
a little bit more deeply

00:36:02.230 --> 00:36:06.350
into these questions, as
you know, with (mumbles)

00:36:06.350 --> 00:36:08.420
and many other colleagues,
we've been looking

00:36:08.420 --> 00:36:10.870
at local-led responses to displacement

00:36:10.870 --> 00:36:14.750
over the course of four years
and then fortunately, COVID

00:36:14.750 --> 00:36:17.180
has hit us right at the end of the project

00:36:17.180 --> 00:36:19.390
but it really draws out the extent

00:36:19.390 --> 00:36:23.970
to which members of of the
camp community of all ages,

00:36:23.970 --> 00:36:26.250
of all professions and of non,

00:36:26.250 --> 00:36:29.440
take different responsibilities
and make different decisions

00:36:29.440 --> 00:36:33.233
on how to respond to these
overlapping precarities.

00:36:34.661 --> 00:36:37.547
I haven't answered your question
